<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-2096] name ofd device type "ofd" instead of "obdfilter"</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-2096</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The current ofd module registers itself as "obdfilter" in order to allow test scripts and /proc entries to be compatible.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, in the long term this should be changed to "ofd" for clarity, and a symlink can be created in /proc/fs/lustre "obdfilter -&amp;gt; ofd" (as osp does for osc /proc files) so that monitoring scripts and older tests (in compat mode) can continue to access the /proc files, but there is a clear separation between the two modules.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment />
